# Why: Rebrand the email footer from upstream Documenso defaults to Pacta.
#      Three logical changes in template-footer.tsx:
#
#        1. "Powered by Documenso" link text → "Powered by Pacta", with
#           the href pointing to https://bizrethink.ai instead of
#           https://documen.so/mail-footer.
#        2. Link color flips from Documenso's `#7AC455` (green) to
#           charcoal `#1f2937` matching Pacta's neutral palette.
#        3. Address fallback (when an org has brandingEnabled=false OR
#           no brandingCompanyDetails set): "Documenso, Inc. / 2261
#           Market Street, San Francisco, CA 94114, USA" →
#           "BizRethink AI (Server Baba Inc.) / Florida, USA".
#
#      The Pacta product name + parent brand are read from APP_NAME and
#      APP_PARENT_BRAND constants in packages/lib/constants/app.ts
#      (added via overlay 021). Future renames are a one-file change.
#
#      What stays unchanged: the brandingEnabled / brandingHidePoweredBy
#      gating logic. Tenants that set their own brandingCompanyDetails
#      see THEIR address; tenants that haven't yet (or have branding
#      disabled) see the BizRethink fallback above.
#
# Why-not-additive: template-footer.tsx is rendered inline by every
#      email template through the upstream <TemplateFooter> component.
#      There's no theme/branding hook upstream that we could intercept
#      from a separate package. Inline patch is unavoidable.
#
# Upstream-merge-fragility: LOW.
#      template-footer.tsx is touched ~1×/quarter upstream. Most upstream
#      changes are biome lint reformatting of className strings, which
#      this patch absorbs into its `+++` side. The 3 functional changes
#      anchor on stable wrapping `<Link>` + `<Text>` components.
#
# Status: REGENERATED 2026-05-25 (v2). v1 patch was truncated at line 31
#         with a "(full file diff — see commit)" placeholder rather than
#         the actual diff body. Regenerated fresh against current
#         upstream/main vs main. Pairs with E8 Playwright spec that
#         asserts Pacta footer wording survives in actual outbound emails
#         via the Inbucket test mailer.

